/pull/109357#issuecomment-3161554424","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109357","id":3161554424,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68cX34","user":{"login":"WhalesState","id":53877170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUzODc3MTcw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/53877170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState","html_url":"https://github.com/WhalesState","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/WhalesState/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T20:45:38Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T20:45:38Z","body":"I have tried to do this before and I didn't like the `+` sign for Forward+, that's why i have used a `-` sign for Compatibility instead.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"477\" height=\"132\" alt=\"Screenshot From 2025-08-06 21-09-20\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/809dcef2-ef58-4915-954a-fdb053fe39b2\" />\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3161554424/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3161903831","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109357#issuecomment-3161903831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109357","id":3161903831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68dtLX","user":{"login":"passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar","html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-06T23:24:16Z","updated_at":"2025-08-06T23:24:16Z","body":"I agree with [Clay's comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103042#issuecomment-2670879136) and with [syntaxerror's comment](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109357#issuecomment-3160709227), unless switching between renderers mid-project is a common operation the button is probably not needed. You'd expect a very visible top-level button to support a common workflow, if it's not the case it adds unnecessary UX friction","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3161903831/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3162029133","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109357#issuecomment-3162029133","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109357","id":3162029133,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68eLxN","user":{"login":"Meorge","id":9957987,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk5NTc5ODc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9957987?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge","html_url":"https://github.com/Meorge","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Meorge/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-07T00:33:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T00:33:09Z","body":"> macOS network icons style? It won't be easy to make it clear enough with 16×16 monochrome icons.\r\n\r\nDefinitely, yeah. I think it could be more feasible by exaggerating the monitor types used - an old, closer-to-square monitor [like this](https://www.gettyimages.com/detail/illustration/old-computer-monitor-royalty-free-illustration/165761919) could work for Compatibility, while a wider monitor [like this](https://stock.adobe.com/images/computer-monitor-screen-flat-icon-for-apps-and-websites/96286992) could be Forward+. The former isn't super representative of the kinds of hardware it'd be likely to run on, and I could see some people feeling mildly insulted about their rendering method being represented by a \"ye olde\" computer. But at such a small icon size, we'd need that difference in shape to be very clear.\r\n\r\n> I have tried to do this before and I didn't like the `+` sign for Forward+, that's why i have used a `-` sign for Compatibility instead.\r\n\r\nAdmittedly, it didn't even cross my mind that the Compatibility icon had a minus in it; I just saw it as some kind of an abstract mark. 😅 IMO a minus doesn't really make sense for \"Compatibility\" anyways, since it supports a *wider* variety of devices than Forward+ (albeit with fewer graphics features), and doesn't have a minus in its name. \r\n\r\n> unless switching between renderers mid-project is a common operation the button is probably not needed\r\n\r\nI do agree with this, yeah – in my experience, the renderer is something that tends to get set once at the beginning of a project, and then isn't (or is *very rarely*) touched again. If there are people who toggle renderer modes more frequently, perhaps it could be made into a setting whether to appear in the top corner or at the bottom? Or always keep it at the bottom, and have a setting to toggle its visibility at the top?\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3162029133/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3162496867","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/109357#issuecomment-3162496867","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109357","id":3162496867,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc68f99j","user":{"login":"bruvzg","id":7645683,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2NDU2ODM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7645683?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg","html_url":"https://github.com/bruvzg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bruvzg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-07T05:08:06Z","updated_at":"2025-08-07T05:08:06Z","body":"> Definitely, yeah. I think it could be more feasible by exaggerating the monitor types used - an old, closer-to-square monitor [like this](https://www.gettyimages.com/detail/illustration/old-computer-monitor-royalty-free-illustration/165761919) could work for Compatibility, while a wider monitor [like this](https://stock.adobe.com/images/computer-monitor-screen-flat-icon-for-apps-and-websites/96286992) could be Forward+. The former isn't super representative of the kinds of hardware it'd be likely to run on, and I could see some people feeling mildly insulted about their rendering method being represented by a \"ye olde\" computer. But at such a small icon size, we'd need that difference in shape to be very clear.\r\n\r\nIn case of macOS icons, the colors and contrast, not the shape (blue screen and beige border vs. bright screen and black border) probably make it more clear at a small size.\r\n\r\n| <img width=\"959\" height=\"425\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-06 at 23 18 11\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7f492b60-a668-4e95-b719-f48a03a31de9\" /> | <img width=\"29\" height=\"90\" alt=\"Screenshot 2025-08-06 at 23 27 58\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/02ff043a-9317-4b84-a231-d9b85d3d6b14\" /> |\r\n|---|---|\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godoteng